# Private workspace guide

This directory is the ignored, local memory layer for one person. It is created by
`./cv init` and must never be committed or used as a public template source.

## Canonical files

- `master_cv.yaml`: lifelong career memory. Only eligible entries in
  `claim_registry` may supply factual résumé prose.
- `applications.yaml`: application stages and outcomes.
- `profile_catalog.yaml`: optional reference-profile classification.

## Subdirectories

- `applications/<id>/`: one exact JD and its decision/claim manifest.
- `evidence/`: durable private proof such as degree records, contracts,
  certificates, thesis source, and historical source material.
- `inventory/`: dated discovery snapshots from GitHub or technical environments.
  Inventory is not résumé evidence until reviewed.
- `audits/`: dated private analyses and reconciliation reports.

Generated contexts and PDFs belong in `../build/`; disposable render output belongs
in `../tmp/`; editable application snapshots belong in `../profiles/`; closed history
belongs in `../archive/`. Run `./cv status` before beginning a new application.
